{"title": "Schwinger (Tapestry Crochet Panel)", "pattern_type": "tapestry", "difficulty": "intermediate", "finished_size_cm": "24 x 32 (chart area about 22 x 30, plus a 2-round border)", "yarn_note": "Made with light (DK, CYC 3) yarn and a 4.0 mm hook at a gauge of about 18 sc and 20 rows = 10 cm, so the 40 x 60 st chart measures about 22 x 30 cm before the border. A thinner yarn makes the panel smaller and a thicker yarn makes it larger, so please crochet a gauge swatch first.", "materials": {"yarn": [{"color": "A - Dark moss grey", "hex": "#6e6f61", "amount_g": 20}, {"color": "B - Stone grey", "hex": "#a1a19c", "amount_g": 11}, {"color": "C - Light dove grey", "hex": "#d7d6d2", "amount_g": 9}, {"color": "D - Taupe", "hex": "#9d896f", "amount_g": 4}, {"color": "E - Walnut brown", "hex": "#8f7357", "amount_g": 3}, {"color": "F - Slate blue", "hex": "#79889c", "amount_g": 2}], "hook_mm": 4.0, "other": ["tapestry needle for weaving in ends", "blocking mat and pins", "optional: picture frame or backing board"]}, "abbreviations": {"ch": "chain", "sc": "single crochet", "sl st": "slip stitch", "sts": "stitches", "Rnd": "round", "RS": "right side", "WS": "wrong side"}, "parts": [{"name": "Foundation", "color": "Colour of the first chart stitch (see chart)", "steps": [{"step": "Foundation", "instruction": "Leaving a 10 cm tail, ch 41 with the colour of the first stitch of chart row 1.", "stitch_count": 41}, {"step": "Row 1 setup", "instruction": "Sc in the 2nd ch from the hook and in each ch across. This gives you the 40 sts of chart row 1. Follow the chart colours from the first stitch, and see 'Chart rows' below for the colour changes.", "stitch_count": 40}]}, {"name": "Chart rows", "color": "A, B, C, D, E, F as shown in the chart", "steps": [{"step": "Reading the chart", "instruction": "Read the chart from the bottom up. Odd rows are RS rows and are read from right to left. Even rows are WS rows and are read from left to right. Each square is 1 sc. Ch 1 at the end of each row and turn. This turning ch does not count as a stitch.", "stitch_count": 40}, {"step": "Changing colour", "instruction": "Change colour in the last step of the sc before the new colour: pull the new colour through the last 2 loops on the hook. Lay the unused colour along the top of the previous row and crochet over it, so the yarn is carried inside the stitches.", "stitch_count": 40}, {"step": "Carrying yarn", "instruction": "Carry a colour that appears again within about 6 sts. For longer gaps, drop it and pick it up again where it is needed, or use a separate small ball. Twist the yarns at each change so there are no holes.", "stitch_count": 40}, {"step": "Rows 1-60", "instruction": "Work all 60 chart rows in sc, following the colour runs printed below. Every row has 40 sc.", "stitch_count": 40}]}, {"name": "Border", "color": "A", "steps": [{"step": "Rnd 1", "instruction": "With RS facing, join A in a top corner. Ch 1, then work 40 sc across the top, 3 sc in the corner, 60 sc evenly down the side (1 per row end), 3 sc in the corner, 40 sc across the foundation edge, 3 sc in the corner, 60 sc up the other side, 3 sc in the last corner. Sl st to the first sc.", "stitch_count": 212}, {"step": "Rnd 2", "instruction": "Ch 1, sc in each sc around. Work 3 sc in the middle sc of each 3-sc corner group. Sl st to the first sc and fasten off.", "stitch_count": 220}]}], "assembly": ["Weave in all ends with a tapestry needle, running them through stitches of the same colour on the WS.", "Wet-block or steam-block the panel to size, pinning it flat so the edges are straight.", "Mount the finished panel on a backing board or frame, or sew a hanging loop to the top border."], "notes": "Keep your tension even when carrying yarn, because tight floats pucker the picture. Keep the same colour on top as you carry across rows, and hold the carried yarn loosely along the previous row. Mark the right-hand edge of the chart so you do not lose your place. Check the chart colours again